<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves fall to $1.78 bln in Feb.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves fall to $1.78 bln in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's net international reserves fell 10.7 percent, or $215 million, to $1.781 billion in February, a government official said Monday.</p>
<p>Reserves were down $235 million from February 1996.</p>
<p>According to the official, who requested anonymity, the reserves fall was due to foreign debt payments.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
